Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Monte Carlo Uncertainty", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"da86af1d-cc24-4bac-91b3-a752f7340bc0"],

Cell["\<\
The default ranges sample mb, mc, G2, G3, M2, and s0. Replace any {min,max} \
pair with a single number to hold that parameter fixed. The fast default \
keeps G3 out of the Monte Carlo scan; switch IncludeG3 to True later if \
needed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7972cdb7-f301-4298-8d28-25d1876049da"],

Cell["\<\
Edit this control block for uncertainty studies. nSamples is the number of \
accepted random points, histBins is the histogram bin count, and Seed fixes \
the random-number sequence so the same cell is reproducible. The result is \
called uncertaintyRun to avoid confusion with the charm-quark mass mc.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"08ed50b9-ca93-4a4b-b186-9cc04934bb69"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData["$BcMixingDefaultUncertaintyRanges"], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[249]:=",ExpressionUUID->"77894a1c-4add-4afb-93a0-5980738ba44f"],

